      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-59594",
      ":question/problem": "![](images/bf/bf86e9ff213dd8685ea2ebe5104f8b31904a9a9f155c055ec76eb776286ba50a.png)\n\nThe graph above shows the number of $A$'s achieved versus the number of hours of exercise for a group of $5$ students in a particular week. Which of the following statements are true?\n\n1. Edward exercised for $3$ hours.\n2. The person who has the greatest number of $A$'s exercised for $6$ hours.\n3. John and Rose exercised for the same amount of time."
